cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use tcmnetpharma in your research, please cite this software and the
  runtime dataset it consumes (see references below).
title: >-
  tcmnetpharma: multi-source Traditional Chinese Medicine network pharmacology
  analysis toolkit
abstract: >-
  An R package for Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) network pharmacology
  analysis. It integrates ten upstream sources into a single herb-molecule-target
  knowledge base: TCMSP, HERB 2.0, BATMAN-TCM 2.0, ETCM2, ChEMBL 37, STRING 12,
  TRRUST v2, Open Targets Platform 25.06 and SymMap V2, plus offline gene sets
  from WikiPathways, Reactome and Gene Ontology. The 2025 edition of the Chinese
  Pharmacopoeia is used as a nomenclature and property reference only and is not
  redistributed. The package provides network, enrichment and module
  visualisation modules.
